---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Write for Us"
  description="Write for CricBreakdown. Share original cricket analysis, features, statistics, history and well-researched stories with our readers."
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pt-16 pb-20">
    <span class="stat-chip text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[#E94560]">Contribute</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl md:text-5xl text-[#1A1A2E] mt-3">Write for Us</h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-ink/65 leading-relaxed mt-6">
      Are you passionate about cricket and enjoy turning your knowledge into clear,
      well-researched stories? CricBreakdown welcomes writers who can bring fresh
      perspectives, useful analysis and strong cricket storytelling to our readers.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-10">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-4">What We Publish</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          We focus on original cricket content that gives readers more than a basic
          scoreline or surface-level summary. Topics can include:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink/70 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Cricket analysis and tactical breakdowns</li>
          <li>IPL and international cricket stories</li>
          <li>Statistical and data-led pieces</li>
          <li>Cricket history and team retrospectives</li>
          <li>Player and team features</li>
          <li>Auction, squad-building and strategy analysis</li>
          <li>Listicles and other useful cricket explainers</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-4">Content Guidelines</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">1. Write original, useful content</h3>
            <p>
              Your article should offer genuine value to the reader. Avoid rewriting
              existing articles or simply repeating information that is already widely available.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">2. Back claims with facts</h3>
            <p>
              Use reliable statistics, records, data and clearly attributable sources
              wherever they strengthen your argument. Accuracy matters more than filling space.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">3. Keep paragraphs readable</h3>
            <p>
              Keep paragraphs concise and consistent so the article is easy to read on
              both desktop and mobile. Break up long sections instead of creating large blocks of text.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">4. Use clear subheadings</h3>
            <p>
              Structure longer pieces with descriptive subheadings. Build the article logically,
              moving from the main question or idea through the supporting evidence to a clear conclusion.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">5. Attribute sources and quotes</h3>
            <p>
              If you use information or quotations from another publication, interview or press conference,
              identify the source clearly. Do not present another outlet's reporting as your own.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">6. Proofread before submitting</h3>
            <p>
              Check your facts, spelling, grammar, links and formatting before sending your work.
              A clean, well-edited submission makes the review process much easier.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-2">7. Plan longer articles</h3>
            <p>
              For detailed pieces, create a simple outline before writing. Give the article a clear direction,
              build interest as you go and finish with a conclusion that answers the central question.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-4">Before You Submit</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-ink/70 list-disc pl-5">
          <li>The article should be original and written specifically for CricBreakdown.</li>
          <li>Do not submit copied, spun or AI-generated content without substantial human editing and verification.</li>
          <li>Check names, statistics, dates and other factual details carefully.</li>
          <li>Include sources for important claims where appropriate.</li>
          <li>Choose a clear topic and make sure the article has a distinct purpose.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-xl bg-white border border-[#e3e7ee] p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold text-[#1A1A2E] mb-4">How to Apply</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
          Send us an original sample that best demonstrates your cricket knowledge and writing ability.
          Include a short introduction about yourself, the topic you would like to write about and your sample article.
        </p>
        <a
          href="mailto:bansar582@gmail.com?subject=CricBreakdown%20Write%20for%20Us%20Submission"
          class="inline-flex mt-6 bg-[#E94560] text-white px-5 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold hover:bg-[#C73652] transition-colors"
        >
          Email Your Submission →
        </a>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink/55">
          Email: <a href="mailto:bansar582@gmail.com" class="text-[#E94560] hover:underline">bansar582@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
